# plan.md §21.5 item 1. QueryLens is a client-side multi-page app: every route
# except `/` (the stage explainers, `/examples`, and the integrated docs under
# `/docs/*`) is drawn by React Router, not by a file on disk. A hard load of
# one of those paths — a refresh, a shared link, a new tab — needs an SPA
# rewrite to `index.html` or it matches no asset. The whole distribution model
# is a shared link (§14.1, §19.3), so that was the original deploy-day
# blocker this file closed.
#
# The rewrite used to live here, as `/*  /index.html  200` — moved to
# `wrangler.jsonc`'s `assets.not_found_handling: "single-page-application"`
# instead, because that rule and this platform's own automatic `.html`/
# `index` URL normalization formed a genuine redirect cycle: Cloudflare's
# deploy validator refused to publish, citing "Infinite loop detected in this
# rule. This would cause a redirect to strip '.html' or '/index'...". The
# native mechanism replaces it without hitting that cycle, and is scoped to
# navigation requests only rather than every unmatched path.
#
# `404.html` stays the last resort — reached when the app bundle itself fails
# to load, not for ordinary unknown routes, which React Router's `*` route
# renders as `NotFoundPage` inside the loaded app.
